/**
 * @description Creates Accounts and their related Contacts through a single
 *              fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork commit. No direct DML is performed here.
 */
public inherited sharing class AccountOnboardingService {

    /**
     * @description Creates one Account per map key and one Contact per last name
     *              in the corresponding list. All records are registered on a
     *              single fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork and committed once.
     * @param  contactLastNamesByAccountName Map of Account Name -> list of Contact
     *               LastNames. Null or empty input returns an empty list and
     *               performs no writes.
     * @return The newly created Accounts (with Ids populated after commit).
     */
    public static List<Account> createAccountsWithContacts(Map<String, List<String>> contactLastNamesByAccountName) {
        List<Account> newAccounts = new List<Account>();

        // Nothing to do: no unit of work, no DML.
        if (contactLastNamesByAccountName == null || contactLastNamesByAccountName.isEmpty()) {
            return newAccounts;
        }

        // Single unit of work tracking both object types; commit happens once.
        fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork uow = new fflib_SObjectUnitOfWork(
            new List<SObjectType>{ Account.SObjectType, Contact.SObjectType }
        );

        for (String accountName : contactLastNamesByAccountName.keySet()) {
            // Account.Name is required; skip null keys rather than failing the whole transaction.
            if (accountName == null) {
                continue;
            }

            Account account = new Account(Name = accountName);
            uow.registerNew(account);
            newAccounts.add(account);

            List<String> lastNames = contactLastNamesByAccountName.get(accountName);
            if (lastNames == null) {
                continue;
            }

            for (String lastName : lastNames) {
                // Contact.LastName is required; skip null entries to keep the commit valid.
                if (lastName == null) {
                    continue;
                }

                Contact contact = new Contact(LastName = lastName);
                // Register the relationship so the UoW resolves Contact.AccountId
                // after the parent Account has been inserted and received its Id.
                uow.registerNew(contact, Contact.AccountId, account);
            }
        }

        // Commit once; only if there is actually something to persist.
        if (!newAccounts.isEmpty()) {
            uow.commitWork();
        }

        // commitWork() populated the Ids on the registered Account instances.
        return newAccounts;
    }
}
```

Here are both files. The service uses the fflib Unit of Work's `registerEvent` support: events registered on the UoW are published by `commitWork` only **after** the DML has been committed, so a failed opportunity update throws before any `Deal_Won__e` is published. Since `registerEvent` does not require the event SObject type to be declared in the factory, `Application.cls` needs no functional change (I've left it as-is).

