public with sharing class ContactPhoneCleanup {

    /**
     * Normalizes the Phone field of the given contacts so it contains only
     * digits and '+' characters. Contacts without a phone are not updated.
     *
     * @param contactIds up to 200 contact Ids (bulk-safe: one query, one DML)
     * @return map of contact Id -> first error message for records that
     *         could not be saved; empty when all saves succeeded
     */
    public static Map<Id, String> normalizePhones(List<Id> contactIds) {
        Map<Id, String> errorsByContactId = new Map<Id, String>();

        if (contactIds == null || contactIds.isEmpty()) {
            return errorsByContactId;
        }

        // Single SOQL for the whole batch (no queries in loops).
        List<Contact> contacts = [
            SELECT Id, Phone
            FROM Contact
            WHERE Id IN :contactIds
        ];

        List<Contact> toUpdate = new List<Contact>();
        for (Contact c : contacts) {
            if (String.isNotBlank(c.Phone)) {
                // Strip everything that is not a digit or '+'.
                c.Phone = c.Phone.replaceAll('[^0-9+]', '');
                toUpdate.add(c);
            }
            // Contacts without a phone are left out of the update entirely.
        }

        if (toUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            return errorsByContactId;
        }

        // allOrNone = false: a validation failure on one record does not block the rest.
        List<Database.SaveResult> results = Database.update(toUpdate, false);

        // Results are returned in the same order as the input records.
        for (Integer i = 0; i < results.size(); i++) {
            if (!results[i].getSuccess()) {
                errorsByContactId.put(
                    toUpdate[i].Id,
                    results[i].getErrors()[0].getMessage()
                );
            }
        }

        return errorsByContactId;
    }
}
```

Notes on the small changes I made to your approach (all deliberate, none change the behavior you asked for):

1. **Query filter + `isNotBlank` guard:** I fetch all requested contacts in one SOQL and only add contacts with a non-blank `Phone` to the update list. "Left out" is implemented by excluding them from the DML entirely, so records without a phone are never touched (no empty-field overwrite, no spurious `LastModifiedDate` bump), and the results list indices stay aligned with the records actually sent.

2. **Empty-batch guards:** The method returns early for a null/empty Id list and when no contact qualifies, avoiding a pointless (even if harmless) DML call. This keeps it safe for callers that pass whatever list they have on hand.

3. **`with sharing`:** Added so the method respects org sharing by default; it also works if you later expose it via `@InvocableMethod` or a REST surface.

One caveat worth knowing: the spec "remove every character that is not a digit or `+`" will keep *internal* plus signs too (e.g. `+44+20...` stays `+44+2018`). If the dialer truly only accepts a *leading* plus, a stricter post-processing step (e.g. keep `+` only at index 0) would be needed — I implemented the rule exactly as you stated it, but say the word and I'll tighten it.

